IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc26-interpretation`

-- ccc26-reports.l4 -- sections 720 to 722.2 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: sentencing proceedings, delay for court-supervised
-- programs, the probation officer's report, the victim impact statement and the community impact statement (lines 15310-15376 of the text).
-- Layer 1 of part ccc26. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Duties that carry a time limit are also written as regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN ...), run with #TRACE in the tests file; the
-- same duty is a decision function beside each. "As soon as practicable" and "as soon as feasible" are open-textured: the number of days is an input.

§ `Section 720 -- Sentencing proceedings; court-supervised programs`

-- src:15310 | Procedure and Evidence
-- src:15311 | Sentencing proceedings
-- src:15312 | 720 (1) A court shall, as soon as practicable after an offender has been found guilty, conduct proceedings to determine the appropriate sentence to be imposed.
@ref s 720(1) (src:15310-15312)
DECLARE `s 720(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 720(1) conduct proceedings to determine the appropriate sentence`

@ref s 720(1) (src:15310-15312)
GIVEN `the offender has been found guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days within which it is practicable to conduct the proceedings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 720(1) action`
`s 720(1) the court's duty to conduct sentencing proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the offender has been found guilty`
    THEN PARTY `the court` MUST `s 720(1) conduct proceedings to determine the appropriate sentence`
         WITHIN `the number of days within which it is practicable to conduct the proceedings`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "no proceedings to determine the appropriate sentence were conducted as soon as practicable after the finding of guilt"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 720(1) (src:15310-15312)
GIVEN `the offender has been found guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(1) the court must conduct proceedings to determine the appropriate sentence` MEANS
    IF `the offender has been found guilty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after an offender has been found guilty"

-- (2): a grant ("The court may ... delay sentencing") with the consents and the considering as conditions of the kind "with" and "after".
-- src:15313 | Court-supervised programs
-- src:15314 | (2) The court may, with the consent of the Attorney General and the offender and after considering the interests of justice and of any victim of the offence, delay sentencing to enable the offender to participate in, under the supervision of the court,
-- src:15315 | (a) a treatment program approved by the province, such as an addiction treatment program or a domestic violence counselling program; or
-- src:15316 | (b) a restorative justice process, as defined in section 715.44, approved by the province.
@ref s 720(2) (src:15313-15316)
GIVEN `s 2 Attorney General: the person who consented is the Attorney General` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that person has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has considered the interests of justice and of any victim of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delay is to enable the offender to take part, under the supervision of the court, in a treatment program approved by the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delay is to enable the offender to take part, under the supervision of the court, in a restorative justice process, as defined in section 715.44, approved by the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(2) the court may delay sentencing` MEANS   -- gate: with
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Attorney General: the person who consented is the Attorney General` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is the Attorney General for this proceeding is for section 2
        IF    (NOT ((`s 2 Attorney General: the person who consented is the Attorney General` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `that person has consented`))
           OR (NOT `the offender consents`)
           OR (NOT `the court has considered the interests of justice and of any victim of the offence`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the consent of the Attorney General and the offender and after considering the interests of justice and of any victim of the offence"
        IF    `the delay is to enable the offender to take part, under the supervision of the court, in a treatment program approved by the province`
           OR `the delay is to enable the offender to take part, under the supervision of the court, in a restorative justice process, as defined in section 715.44, approved by the province`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "delay sentencing to enable the offender to participate in, under the supervision of the court, (a) a treatment program approved by the province, such as an addiction treatment program or a domestic violence counselling program; or (b) a restorative justice process"

§ `Section 721 -- Report by probation officer`

-- (1): the probation officer's duty, "if required to do so by a court", for an accused "other than an organization" who pleads guilty or is found guilty.
-- src:15317 | Report by probation officer
-- src:15318 | 721 (1) Subject to regulations made under subsection (2), where an accused, other than an organization, pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence, a probation officer shall, if required to do so by a court, prepare and file with the court a report in writing relating to the accused for the purpose of assisting the court in imposing a sentence or in determining whether the accused should be discharged under section 730.
@ref s 721(1) (src:15317-15318)
GIVEN `the accused is an organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court requires the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(1) the probation officer must prepare and file a report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused is an organization` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where an accused, other than an organization, pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence"
        IF NOT `the accused pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an accused, other than an organization, pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence"
        IF NOT `a court requires the report` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if required to do so by a court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2) lets a province make regulations about the offences for which a court may require a report and the report's content and form: machinery.

-- (3): the matters a report must contain, "Unless otherwise specified by the court" and "wherever possible".
-- src:15321 | Content of report
-- src:15322 | (3) Unless otherwise specified by the court, the report must, wherever possible, contain information on the following matters:
-- src:15323 | (a) the offender’s age, maturity, character, behaviour, attitude and willingness to make amends;
-- src:15324 | (b) subject to subsection 119(2) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act, the history of previous dispositions under the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985, the history of previous sentences under the Youth Criminal Justice Act, and of previous findings of guilt under this Act and any other Act of Parliament;
-- src:15325 | (c) the history of any alternative measure or restorative justice process, as those terms are defined in section 715.44, that is used to deal with the offender, and the offender’s response to those measures; and
-- src:15326 | (d) any matter required, by any regulation made under subsection (2), to be included in the report.
@ref s 721(3) (src:15321-15326)
DECLARE `s 721(3) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 721(3)(a) the offender's age, maturity, character, behaviour, attitude and willingness to make amends`
    `s 721(3)(b) the history of previous dispositions under the Young Offenders Act, of previous sentences under the Youth Criminal Justice Act, and of previous findings of guilt under this Act and any other Act of Parliament`
    `s 721(3)(c) the history of any alternative measure or restorative justice process that is used to deal with the offender, and the offender's response`
    `s 721(3)(d) any matter required, by a regulation made under subsection (2), to be included in the report`
    `s 721(3) another matter`

@ref s 721(3) (src:15321-15326)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 721(3) matter`
      `the court specified otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is possible to give the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 119(2) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act allows the history to be given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(3) the report must contain information on the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF matter EQUALS `s 721(3) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "on the following matters"
        IF `the court specified otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise specified by the court"
        IF NOT `it is possible to give the information` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wherever possible"
        IF matter EQUALS `s 721(3)(b) the history of previous dispositions under the Young Offenders Act, of previous sentences under the Youth Criminal Justice Act, and of previous findings of guilt under this Act and any other Act of Parliament` AND (NOT `subsection 119(2) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act allows the history to be given`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to subsection 119(2) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15327 | Idem
-- src:15328 | (4) The report must also contain information on any other matter required by the court, after hearing argument from the prosecutor and the offender, to be included in the report, subject to any contrary regulation made under subsection (2).
@ref s 721(4) (src:15327-15328)
GIVEN `the court requires the matter to be included in the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard argument from the prosecutor and the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation made under subsection 721(2) provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(4) the report must also contain information on the other matter` MEANS
    IF     `the court requires the matter to be included in the report`
       AND `the court has heard argument from the prosecutor and the offender`
       AND (NOT `a regulation made under subsection 721(2) provides to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other matter required by the court, after hearing argument from the prosecutor and the offender, to be included in the report, subject to any contrary regulation"

-- src:15329 | Copy of report
-- src:15330 | (5) The clerk of the court shall provide a copy of the report, as soon as practicable after filing, to the offender or counsel for the offender, as directed by the court, and to the prosecutor.
@ref s 721(5) (src:15329-15330)
DECLARE `s 721(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 721(5) provide a copy of the report to the offender or counsel for the offender, as the court directs, and to the prosecutor`

@ref s 721(5) (src:15329-15330)
GIVEN `the report has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days within which it is practicable to provide the copy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 721(5) action`
`s 721(5) the clerk's duty to provide a copy of the report` MEANS
    IF `the report has been filed`
    THEN PARTY `the clerk of the court` MUST `s 721(5) provide a copy of the report to the offender or counsel for the offender, as the court directs, and to the prosecutor`
         WITHIN `the number of days within which it is practicable to provide the copy`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the clerk of the court` BECAUSE "no copy of the report was provided as soon as practicable after filing"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 721(5) (src:15329-15330)
GIVEN `the report has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(5) the clerk must provide a copy of the report` MEANS
    IF `the report has been filed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable after filing"

§ `Section 722 -- Victim impact statement`

-- (1): the court shall consider a statement of a victim. "Victim" is s 2's, answered for the purpose of section 722 (a seam input).
-- src:15331 | Victim impact statement
-- src:15332 | 722 (1) When determining the sentence to be imposed on an offender or determining whether the offender should be discharged under section 730 in respect of any offence, the court shall consider any statement of a victim prepared in accordance with this section and filed with the court describing the physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss suffered by the victim as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the victim.
@ref s 722(1) (src:15331-15332)
GIVEN `the court is determining the sentence to be imposed on an offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 victim: the purpose is section 722` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement was prepared in accordance with section 722 and filed with the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement describes the physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss suffered by the victim as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(1) the court must consider the statement of the victim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is determining the sentence to be imposed on an offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When determining the sentence to be imposed on an offender or determining whether the offender should be discharged under section 730"
        IF `s 2 victim: the purpose is section 722` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the author is a victim for section 722 is for section 2
        IF `s 2 victim: the purpose is section 722` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any statement of a victim"
        IF NOT `the statement was prepared in accordance with section 722 and filed with the court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any statement of a victim prepared in accordance with this section and filed with the court"
        IF NOT `the statement describes the physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss suffered by the victim as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the victim` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "describing the physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss suffered by the victim"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15333 | Inquiry by court
-- src:15334 | (2) As soon as feasible after a finding of guilt and in any event before imposing sentence, the court shall inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps have been taken to provide the victim with an opportunity to prepare a statement referred to in subsection (1).
@ref s 722(2) (src:15333-15334)
DECLARE `s 722(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 722(2) inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps have been taken to provide the victim with an opportunity to prepare a statement`

@ref s 722(2) (src:15333-15334)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from the finding of guilt until the sentence is imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 722(2) action`
`s 722(2) the court's duty to inquire of the prosecutor` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN PARTY `the court` MUST `s 722(2) inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps have been taken to provide the victim with an opportunity to prepare a statement`
         WITHIN `the number of days from the finding of guilt until the sentence is imposed`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not inquire before imposing sentence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 722(2) (src:15333-15334)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As soon as feasible after a finding of guilt and in any event before imposing sentence"

-- (3): a grant ("the court may adjourn") on application or on its own motion, "if the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere".
-- src:15335 | Adjournment
-- src:15336 | (3) On application of the prosecutor or a victim or on its own motion, the court may adjourn the proceedings to permit the victim to prepare a statement referred to in subsection (1) or to present evidence in accordance with subsection (9), if the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 722(3) (src:15335-15336)
GIVEN `the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a victim applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adjournment is to permit the victim to prepare a statement referred to in subsection 722(1) or to present evidence in accordance with subsection 722(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(3) the court may adjourn the proceedings` MEANS   -- gate: on (application or own motion), and if (the court is satisfied)
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prosecutor applies`) AND (NOT `a victim applies`) AND (NOT `the court acts on its own motion`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application of the prosecutor or a victim or on its own motion"
        IF NOT `the adjournment is to permit the victim to prepare a statement referred to in subsection 722(1) or to present evidence in accordance with subsection 722(9)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to permit the victim to prepare a statement referred to in subsection (1) or to present evidence in accordance with subsection (9)"
        IF NOT `the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15337 | Form
-- src:15338 | (4) The statement must be prepared in writing, using Form 34.2 in Part XXVIII, in accordance with the procedures established by a program designated for that purpose by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction.
@ref s 722(4) (src:15337-15338)
GIVEN `the statement is prepared in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement uses Form 34.2 in Part XXVIII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is prepared in accordance with the procedures established by a program designated by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(4) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the statement is prepared in writing`
       AND `the statement uses Form 34.2 in Part XXVIII`
       AND `the statement is prepared in accordance with the procedures established by a program designated by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement must be prepared in writing, using Form 34.2 in Part XXVIII, in accordance with the procedures established by a program designated for that purpose"

-- (5): the court shall permit the victim, on request, to present the statement in the four ways.
-- src:15339 | Presentation of statement
-- src:15340 | (5) The court shall, on the request of a victim, permit the victim to present the statement by
-- src:15341 | (a) reading it;
-- src:15342 | (b) reading it in the presence and close proximity of any support person of the victim’s choice or a support animal;
-- src:15343 | (c) reading it outside the court room or behind a screen or other device that would allow the victim not to see the offender; or
-- src:15344 | (d) presenting it in any other manner that the court considers appropriate.
@ref s 722(5) (src:15339-15344)
DECLARE `s 722(5) manner of presenting the statement` IS ONE OF
    `s 722(5)(a) reading it`
    `s 722(5)(b) reading it in the presence and close proximity of any support person of the victim's choice or a support animal`
    `s 722(5)(c) reading it outside the court room or behind a screen or other device that would allow the victim not to see the offender`
    `s 722(5)(d) presenting it in any other manner`

@ref s 722(5) (src:15339-15344)
GIVEN `the victim requests it` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A `s 722(5) manner of presenting the statement`
      `the court considers the other manner appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(5) the court must permit the victim to present the statement in the manner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the victim requests it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the request of a victim"
        IF manner EQUALS `s 722(5)(d) presenting it in any other manner` AND (NOT `the court considers the other manner appropriate`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "presenting it in any other manner that the court considers appropriate"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (6): the photograph. A grant ("may have with them a photograph") during the presentation, "if it would not, in the opinion of the court, disrupt the proceedings".
-- src:15345 | Photograph
-- src:15346 | (6) During the presentation
-- src:15347 | (a) the victim may have with them a photograph of themselves taken before the commission of the offence if it would not, in the opinion of the court, disrupt the proceedings; or
@ref s 722(6)(a) (src:15345-15347)
GIVEN `the victim is presenting the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the photograph is of the victim, taken before the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that it would disrupt the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(6)(a) the victim may have a photograph of themselves with them` MEANS   -- gate: during (the presentation), and if (it would not disrupt)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the victim is presenting the statement` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "During the presentation"
        IF NOT `the photograph is of the victim, taken before the commission of the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a photograph of themselves taken before the commission of the offence"
        IF `the court is of the opinion that it would disrupt the proceedings` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it would not, in the opinion of the court, disrupt the proceedings"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15348 | (b) if the statement is presented by someone acting on the victim’s behalf, that individual may have with them a photograph of the victim taken before the commission of the offence if it would not, in the opinion of the court, disrupt the proceedings.
@ref s 722(6)(b) (src:15348)
GIVEN `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement is presented by someone acting on the victim's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is presenting the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the photograph is of the victim, taken before the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that it would disrupt the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(6)(b) the individual presenting the statement on the victim's behalf may have a photograph of the victim with them` MEANS   -- gate: during (the presentation), and if (it would not disrupt)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual is presenting the statement` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "During the presentation"
        IF NOT `the statement is presented by someone acting on the victim's behalf` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the statement is presented by someone acting on the victim's behalf, that individual may have with them a photograph of the victim"
        IF `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the individual may act on the victim's behalf is for section 2.2
        IF `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that individual" must be one acting on the victim's behalf
        IF NOT `the photograph is of the victim, taken before the commission of the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a photograph of the victim taken before the commission of the offence"
        IF `the court is of the opinion that it would disrupt the proceedings` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it would not, in the opinion of the court, disrupt the proceedings"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (7): a bar with an "unless": presenting outside the court room needs the closed-circuit or videoconference arrangements and the offender's access to counsel.
-- src:15349 | Conditions of exclusion
-- src:15350 | (7) The victim shall not present the statement outside the court room unless arrangements are made for the offender and the judge or justice to watch the presentation by means of closed-circuit television or videoconference and the offender is permitted to communicate with counsel while watching the presentation.
@ref s 722(7) (src:15349-15350)
GIVEN `the victim presents the statement outside the court room` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arrangements are made for the offender and the judge or justice to watch the presentation by means of closed-circuit television or videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is permitted to communicate with counsel while watching the presentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(7) the victim is barred from presenting the statement outside the court room` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the victim presents the statement outside the court room` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not present the statement outside the court room"
        IF `arrangements are made for the offender and the judge or justice to watch the presentation by means of closed-circuit television or videoconference` AND `the offender is permitted to communicate with counsel while watching the presentation` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless arrangements are made for the offender and the judge or justice to watch the presentation by means of closed-circuit television or videoconference and the offender is permitted to communicate with counsel while watching the presentation"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15351 | Consideration of statement
-- src:15352 | (8) In considering the statement, the court shall take into account the portions of the statement that it considers relevant to the determination referred to in subsection (1) and disregard any other portion.
@ref s 722(8) (src:15351-15352)
GIVEN `the court considers the portion relevant to the determination referred to in subsection 722(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(8) the court must take the portion of the statement into account` MEANS
    IF `the court considers the portion relevant to the determination referred to in subsection 722(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "disregard any other portion"

-- src:15353 | Evidence concerning victim admissible
-- src:15354 | (9) Whether or not a statement has been prepared and filed in accordance with this section, the court may consider any other evidence concerning any victim of the offence for the purpose of determining the sentence to be imposed on the offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730.
@ref s 722(9) (src:15353-15354)
GIVEN `the evidence concerns a victim of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is determining the sentence to be imposed on the offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(9) the court may consider other evidence concerning a victim` MEANS   -- gate: none (whether or not a statement was filed; the limit is on the evidence and the purpose)
    IF `the evidence concerns a victim of the offence` AND `the purpose is determining the sentence to be imposed on the offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other evidence concerning any victim of the offence for the purpose of determining the sentence to be imposed on the offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730"

§ `Section 722.1 -- Copy of statement`

-- src:15355 | Copy of statement
-- src:15356 | 722.1 The clerk of the court shall provide a copy of a statement referred to in subsection 722(1), as soon as practicable after a finding of guilt, to the offender or counsel for the offender, and to the prosecutor.
@ref s 722.1 (src:15355-15356)
DECLARE `s 722.1 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 722.1 provide a copy of the statement to the offender or counsel for the offender, and to the prosecutor`

@ref s 722.1 (src:15355-15356)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days within which it is practicable to provide the copy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 722.1 action`
`s 722.1 the clerk's duty to provide a copy of the statement` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN PARTY `the clerk of the court` MUST `s 722.1 provide a copy of the statement to the offender or counsel for the offender, and to the prosecutor`
         WITHIN `the number of days within which it is practicable to provide the copy`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the clerk of the court` BECAUSE "no copy of the statement was provided as soon as practicable after the finding of guilt"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 722.1 (src:15355-15356)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.1 the clerk must provide a copy of the statement` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable after a finding of guilt"

§ `Section 722.2 -- Community impact statement`

-- src:15357 | Community impact statement
-- src:15358 | 722.2 (1) When determining the sentence to be imposed on an offender or determining whether the offender should be discharged under section 730 in respect of any offence, the court shall consider any statement made by an individual on a community’s behalf that was prepared in accordance with this section and filed with the court describing the harm or loss suffered by the community as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the community.
@ref s 722.2(1) (src:15357-15358)
GIVEN `the court is determining the sentence to be imposed on an offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement was made by an individual on a community's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement was prepared in accordance with section 722.2 and filed with the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement describes the harm or loss suffered by the community as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.2(1) the court must consider the statement made on the community's behalf` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is determining the sentence to be imposed on an offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When determining the sentence to be imposed on an offender or determining whether the offender should be discharged under section 730"
        IF NOT `the statement was made by an individual on a community's behalf` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any statement made by an individual on a community's behalf"
        IF NOT `the statement was prepared in accordance with section 722.2 and filed with the court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that was prepared in accordance with this section and filed with the court"
        IF NOT `the statement describes the harm or loss suffered by the community as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the community` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "describing the harm or loss suffered by the community as the result of the commission of the offence and the impact of the offence on the community"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15359 | Inquiry by court
-- src:15360 | (1.1) As soon as feasible after a finding of guilt and in any event before imposing a sentence, the court shall inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to provide an opportunity for the preparation of a statement referred to in subsection (1).
@ref s 722.2(1.1) (src:15359-15360)
DECLARE `s 722.2(1.1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 722.2(1.1) inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to provide an opportunity for the preparation of a statement`

@ref s 722.2(1.1) (src:15359-15360)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from the finding of guilt until the sentence is imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 722.2(1.1) action`
`s 722.2(1.1) the court's duty to inquire of the prosecutor` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN PARTY `the court` MUST `s 722.2(1.1) inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to provide an opportunity for the preparation of a statement`
         WITHIN `the number of days from the finding of guilt until the sentence is imposed`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not inquire before imposing sentence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 722.2(1.1) (src:15359-15360)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.2(1.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As soon as feasible after a finding of guilt and in any event before imposing a sentence"

-- src:15361 | Adjournment
-- src:15362 | (1.2) On application of the prosecutor or the community or on its own motion, the court may adjourn the proceedings to provide an opportunity for the preparation of a statement referred to in subsection (1) or to present evidence in accordance with subsection (6) if the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 722.2(1.2) (src:15361-15362)
GIVEN `the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the community applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adjournment is to provide an opportunity for the preparation of a statement referred to in subsection 722.2(1) or to present evidence in accordance with subsection 722.2(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.2(1.2) the court may adjourn the proceedings` MEANS   -- gate: on (application or own motion), and if (the court is satisfied)
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prosecutor applies`) AND (NOT `the community applies`) AND (NOT `the court acts on its own motion`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application of the prosecutor or the community or on its own motion"
        IF NOT `the adjournment is to provide an opportunity for the preparation of a statement referred to in subsection 722.2(1) or to present evidence in accordance with subsection 722.2(6)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to provide an opportunity for the preparation of a statement referred to in subsection (1) or to present evidence in accordance with subsection (6)"
        IF NOT `the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15363 | Form
-- src:15364 | (2) The statement must be prepared in writing, using Form 34.3 in Part XXVIII, in accordance with the procedures established by a program designated for that purpose by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction.
@ref s 722.2(2) (src:15363-15364)
GIVEN `the statement is prepared in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement uses Form 34.3 in Part XXVIII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is prepared in accordance with the procedures established by a program designated by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.2(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the statement is prepared in writing`
       AND `the statement uses Form 34.3 in Part XXVIII`
       AND `the statement is prepared in accordance with the procedures established by a program designated by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement must be prepared in writing, using Form 34.3 in Part XXVIII, in accordance with the procedures established by a program designated for that purpose"

-- src:15365 | Presentation of statement
-- src:15366 | (3) The court shall, on the request of the individual making the statement, permit the individual to present the statement by
-- src:15367 | (a) reading it;
-- src:15368 | (b) reading it in the presence and close proximity of any support person of the individual’s choice or a support animal;
-- src:15369 | (c) reading it outside the court room or behind a screen or other device that would allow the individual not to see the offender; or
-- src:15370 | (d) presenting it in any other manner that the court considers appropriate.
@ref s 722.2(3) (src:15365-15370)
DECLARE `s 722.2(3) manner of presenting the statement` IS ONE OF
    `s 722.2(3)(a) reading it`
    `s 722.2(3)(b) reading it in the presence and close proximity of any support person of the individual's choice or a support animal`
    `s 722.2(3)(c) reading it outside the court room or behind a screen or other device that would allow the individual not to see the offender`
    `s 722.2(3)(d) presenting it in any other manner`

@ref s 722.2(3) (src:15365-15370)
GIVEN `the individual making the statement requests it` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A `s 722.2(3) manner of presenting the statement`
      `the court considers the other manner appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.2(3) the court must permit the individual to present the statement in the manner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual making the statement requests it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the request of the individual making the statement"
        IF manner EQUALS `s 722.2(3)(d) presenting it in any other manner` AND (NOT `the court considers the other manner appropriate`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "presenting it in any other manner that the court considers appropriate"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15371 | Conditions of exclusion
-- src:15372 | (4) The individual making the statement shall not present it outside the court room unless arrangements are made for the offender and the judge or justice to watch the presentation by means of closed-circuit television or videoconference and the offender is permitted to communicate with counsel while watching the presentation.
@ref s 722.2(4) (src:15371-15372)
GIVEN `the individual presents the statement outside the court room` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arrangements are made for the offender and the judge or justice to watch the presentation by means of closed-circuit television or videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is permitted to communicate with counsel while watching the presentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.2(4) the individual is barred from presenting the statement outside the court room` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual presents the statement outside the court room` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not present it outside the court room"
        IF `arrangements are made for the offender and the judge or justice to watch the presentation by means of closed-circuit television or videoconference` AND `the offender is permitted to communicate with counsel while watching the presentation` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless arrangements are made for the offender and the judge or justice to watch the presentation by means of closed-circuit television or videoconference and the offender is permitted to communicate with counsel while watching the presentation"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15373 | Copy of statement
-- src:15374 | (5) The clerk of the court shall, as soon as feasible after a finding of guilt, provide a copy of the statement to the offender or counsel for the offender, and to the prosecutor.
@ref s 722.2(5) (src:15373-15374)
DECLARE `s 722.2(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 722.2(5) provide a copy of the statement to the offender or counsel for the offender, and to the prosecutor`

@ref s 722.2(5) (src:15373-15374)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days within which it is feasible to provide the copy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 722.2(5) action`
`s 722.2(5) the clerk's duty to provide a copy of the statement` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN PARTY `the clerk of the court` MUST `s 722.2(5) provide a copy of the statement to the offender or counsel for the offender, and to the prosecutor`
         WITHIN `the number of days within which it is feasible to provide the copy`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the clerk of the court` BECAUSE "no copy of the statement was provided as soon as feasible after the finding of guilt"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 722.2(5) (src:15373-15374)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.2(5) the clerk must provide a copy of the statement` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as feasible after a finding of guilt"

-- src:15375 | Evidence concerning community admissible
-- src:15376 | (6) Whether or not a statement has been prepared and filed in accordance with this section, the court may consider any other evidence concerning the community for the purpose of determining the sentence to be imposed on the offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730.
@ref s 722.2(6) (src:15375-15376)
GIVEN `the evidence concerns the community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is determining the sentence to be imposed on the offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722.2(6) the court may consider other evidence concerning the community` MEANS   -- gate: none (whether or not a statement was filed; the limit is on the evidence and the purpose)
    IF `the evidence concerns the community` AND `the purpose is determining the sentence to be imposed on the offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other evidence concerning the community for the purpose of determining the sentence to be imposed on the offender or whether the offender should be discharged under section 730"
